  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development would result in poor appearance, by virtue of its massing, layout and design, that would adversely impact the character of the locale and Leytonstone Conservation Area. The extensions would represent overdevelopment of the site and appear as an incongruous addition to the host building and streescape. Additionally, the proposed shop frontages would not reflect the character of the retail parade and read as a poor replacement of existing low quality design.&amp;nbsp;The proposals would be contrary to policies 45, 53 and 72 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024) and&amp;nbsp;Supplementary Planning Guidance Shopfront Design Guide (2013).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The scheme fails to provide any soft landscaping or urban greening to contribute to biodiversity and contributes to the harmful visual impact of the development upon the Conservation Area given it&#x27;s visibility within the streetscene as an end of terrace plot. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policies 53, 72 and 79 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed side extension to the existing shop would project into the pavement which is classified as highway in this instance. In accordance with Section 137 of the Highway Act 1980, it is an offence for a person to willfully obstruct a highway without lawful authority. The proposal would result in permanent obstruction to the highway and reduce the pedestrian space available to road users in conflict with Policies 60 and 61 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan Part 1 (2024).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
